<attribute name="version" nodeId="749cd11d"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="86e79415">The RACM provides information on the &lt;a class=&quot;elementLink&quot;
href=&quot;./../../core.gen.concepts.base/guidances/termdefinitions/risk_D388B03E.html&quot; guid=&quot;_8ycBEBCVEeape9rfQ0OXaQ&quot;&gt;risk&lt;/a&gt;s
and associated &lt;a class=&quot;elementLink&quot; href=&quot;./../../core.gen.concepts.base/guidances/termdefinitions/control_2E08BE3A.html&quot;
guid=&quot;_4vBO8BCVEeape9rfQ0OXaQ&quot;&gt;control&lt;/a&gt;s.</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="ef7754bd"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="865804d8">&lt;p&gt;
    Utilizing the matrix, risks should be documented based on frequency, severity and detection. Controls should then be
    evaluated and enhanced to address any residual risk.  A key risk assessment principle is that it should take place
    prior to implementing any changes. Risks should be assessed and control measures and/or mitigating resolution items put
    into action before new work is introduced or systems are changed.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="f294b2e2"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="daf2e260">&lt;p&gt;
    The purpose of this work product is to document risk and controls across various process components.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The risk and controls matrix is used in various stages of the engagement lifecycle. The risk and controls matrix can be
    used to document baseline risks and controls. The baseline risk and controls document can be reviewed and assessed to
    identify gaps and/or improvement opportunities. Finally, the risk and control matrix can also be used to define target
    controls identified in process design tasks and identify any residuals risks associated with those target controls.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="30f19665">&lt;p&gt;
    Impact of not documenting inherent risks and mitigating controls could potentially result in one or more of the
    following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Project failure resulting in unsuccessful processes and / or systems
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Failure to meet end-user and / or external customer needs
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Resistance from stakeholders
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Failure to pass internal and / or external audit
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Regulatory fines&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="6c79a818">&lt;p&gt;
    Under certain circumstances, not documenting risks and controls may be acceptable. The following includes a small set
    of such potential circumstances:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        If the client organization’s Internal Controls and / or Internal Audit teams have already documented inherent risks
        and mitigating controls&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="6f59fb8a">The following information may be captured in the RACM, based on analysis of inputs from the client: 
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control reference
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Process and sub-process
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Activity flow name
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control objective
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control objective assertion
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Risk description
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Risk category (operational, strategic, regulatory, etc.)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Likelihood
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Impact
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Inherent risk ranking
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Cause of assertion impacted
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control group maturity
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Process description
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Recommended control practice description
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Client control description
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control nature
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control category (indirect entry-level, direct entry-level, transaction-level, etc.)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control type (manual,system, IT-dependent)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        System control type
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Frequency of control
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Control evidence
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        IT application module name
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Exception report name
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Exception details
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Vulnerability
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reasonableness and related thresholds
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="35698919">&lt;p&gt;
    There are number of industry standard control notations that can be leveraged when documenting the organizations risk
    and controls. These notations include those provided by the Committee of Sponsoring Organizations of the Treadway
    Commission (COSO), among others. Before leveraging any industry standards, engagement leadership and the client should
    be consulted.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The risk and control matrix is depicted in an Excel format.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="representation" nodeId="471d33c7"></attribute>
